<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Applies on devices older than API 31; data_extraction_rules.xml covers API 31 and above.

  Only the ledger database is backed up. Naming an <include> makes the policy exclusive, so caches,
  logs and every transient file are left out by default rather than by omission.

  The whole `database` domain is included rather than the file name, so renaming the database
  cannot silently stop the backup.

  Be clear about what this does and does not buy. It controls *what* is copied; it does not make it
  private. Android auto-backup is encrypted in transit and at rest by Google, but it is not
  encrypted with a key only you hold, so the ledger does leave the device. Excluding the database
  instead would keep it on the phone and lose it with the phone - keeping the backup is the
  deliberate choice here.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="database" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
